# Azure DevOps — Blog stories

Backlog for this repo lives in **Azure DevOps**, not GitHub Issues (Dependabot / security advisories and automation that already opens GitHub issues may remain there).

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Organization** | `https://dev.azure.com/funkysi1701` |
| **Project** | `My GitHub Projects` |
| **Parent Feature** | **2996** (funkysi1701.com / Hugo blog) |

When the user asks to review open stories, pick next work, or summarize the backlog:

1. Query **User Stories** (and related Tasks/Bugs as needed) under **parent Feature `2996`**.
2. Exclude **Closed** and **Removed**.
3. Prefer `az boards query` with WIQL filtering `[System.Parent] = 2996` (org/project as above).
4. Order by priority then changed date unless the user specifies otherwise.

Example WIQL filter:

```wiql
SELECT [System.Id], [System.Title], [System.State], [System.WorkItemType],
       [Microsoft.VSTS.Common.Priority], [System.Tags], [System.ChangedDate], [System.Parent]
FROM WorkItems
WHERE [System.TeamProject] = 'My GitHub Projects'
  AND [System.WorkItemType] = 'User Story'
  AND [System.State] <> 'Closed'
  AND [System.State] <> 'Removed'
  AND [System.Parent] = 2996
ORDER BY [Microsoft.VSTS.Common.Priority] ASC, [System.ChangedDate] DESC
```

Link pull requests with `AB#{id}` in the **PR description** (not titles only).
